    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "While '安閑' (ankan) can mean 'calm' or 'peaceful' and is grammatically aligned, it is not the most common or natural adjective a general learner would encounter for the broad English concept of 'calm'. It often carries nuances of being undisturbed, at leisure, or even overly relaxed/unconcerned (as per JMdict Sense 1). More common and versatile adjectives like '落ち着いた' (ochitsuita) or '穏やかな' (odayakana) better represent the general sense of 'calm' for a learner.",
